{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And stink.</b> For had it not stunk, they would not have refrained from drinking from it — for even though its appearance was blood, its taste was water; perhaps they would have drunk, just as the nations of the world now eat. Therefore the fish died, in order that the river would stink. And likewise it implies, as it is written further on. And it is difficult for me: if so, why is the plague called only by the name of the blood and not by the name of the stinking? It seems to me: because the stinking is not conspicuous, whereas the blood is conspicuous."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:48.903189523Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}